      "role": "user",
      "content": "we tried a pre-treatment on a test run but it didn't really help. it's still happening in these very specific, random little clusters. it almost feels like something is actively messing with the ink during the press, like it's being snatched away or interrupted right as the heat hits it. i know that sounds crazy but it's so localized it's hard to blame the whole machine. could there be some kind of interference or something i'm missing in the chemical process?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
